my hope is that in listening to either  book people find it reassuring that so  many of the people they might put on a  pedestal have all the same problems that  they do  it's not that they succeed because they  lack insecurities or lack problems or  lack self-defeating habits it's that  they've figured out how to manage those  things these world-class performers  don't have superpowers the rules they've  crafted for themselves allow the bending  of reality to such an extent that it  might seem that way but they've learned  how to do this and so can you these  so-called rules are often uncommon  habits and bigger questions so if you  want to change your life significantly  you want to change your business or  career significantly you want to change  how you relate to other people  significantly the magic is really in the  questions these two books can give you  not just a set toolkit of better  questions but the increased ability to  craft questions of your own they get you  the results you want and that is as  close to a superpower as I think it's  possible in a surprising number of cases  the power is in the absurd the more  absurd the more impossible the question  the more profound the answers  take for instance a question that serial  billionaire Peter Thiel likes to ask  himself and others if you have a ten  year plan of how to get somewhere you  should ask why can't you do this in six  months for purposes of illustration here  I might reword that to what might you do  to accomplish your ten-year goals in the  next six months if you had a gun against  your head I do recommend that everybody  pursue if they can the bare bones of  drawing let's say the bare bones of  music just so they develop greater  sensitivity in  seeing and hearing and listening because  that transfers to everything  animal 1 is 20 minutes of seated  meditation in the morning  remember 2 would be journaling in some  short form isolating the things that are  most important to get done that day the  big dominoes to tip over or if you're  feeling really stressed out morning  pages from Julia Cameron very very  helpful then if I had to pick a third I  would say a short bout of exercise if I  checked those 3 boxes every day feels  more in control  [Music]
 

